{
  "_comment": [
    "M7.1 fixture: the current validation host, roughly as observed.",
    "",
    "Three physical interfaces (two Ethernet, one wireless client), an Ethernet",
    "uplink currently carrying the default route, a spare Ethernet port with no",
    "carrier and no address, plus Docker, Tailscale and container veth",
    "infrastructure.",
    "",
    "Every property M7.1 reasons about is present here: physicality, link kind,",
    "carrier, speed (and the ABSENCE of speed on the spare port), addresses,",
    "route usage and bridge/veth membership. The spare port deliberately has no",
    "'speed' field, because the real host reports none and an analysis that",
    "invented one would be untestable against it.",
    "",
    "Routes live in this same file so link state and routing cannot drift apart:",
    "a fixture with a default route over an interface that has no link would be",
    "testing a host nobody has.",
    "",
    "The IPv6 link-local addresses are here deliberately. Every IPv6-capable host",
    "auto-assigns fe80::/64 on every interface, and an analysis that counted",
    "those as occupancy would report every NIC in the world as in use."
  ],
